\p
\v 41 As he sat¦33386 down¦33386 in¦33390 front¦33390 of¦33390 the \add temple\add* treasury¦33393, Yeshua watched the crowd¦33402 as they threw coins into¦33406 \add the dish\add*, and¦33385 some rich¦33411 people were¦33413 donating quite valuable \add silver\add* coins.
\v 42 Then¦33415 an impoverished widow¦33421 came¦33416 and¦33415 threw¦33423 in two¦33425 small \add copper\add* coins.
\v 43 Yeshua called¦33430 his¦33433 followers¦33432 and¦33429 told them¦33436, “\wj Honestly, that¦33443 poor¦33445 widow¦33442 gave more¦33447 than¦33447 all¦33448 the others.\wj*
\v 44 \wj You see, most people donate from¦33462 their excess wealth¦33463, but¦33470 this¦33469 woman¦33469 even gave \+add some of\+add* the small amount that¦33469 she¦33477 needed to live¦33481 on.\wj*”
\c 13
\s1 Yeshua predicts total destruction of the temple
