\r (Mat. 24:1-2; Luke 21:5-6)
\p
\v 1 As they were leaving the temple¦33488 area, one¦33491 of¦33493 Yeshua's followers¦33494 noted, “Teacher¦33498, look at those \add large, chiselled\add* stones¦33501 and¦33502 the \add beautiful\add* buildings¦33504 \add that they've been made into\add*.”
\p
\v 2 “\wj Yes, incredible buildings¦33522,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* responded¦33512, “\wj but¦33507 \+add the time will come\+add* when they're torn¦33538 down—not a single \+add piece of\+add* stone¦33533 will be left¦33529 sitting in its place.\wj*”
\s1 Yeshua talks about coming hardships
