\r (Mat. 24:29-31; Luke 21:25-28)
\p
\v 24 “\wj After¦34012 those¦34009 very difficult times, the sun¦34017 will¦34018 go dark\x + \xo 13:24: \xt Isa 13:10; Yoel 2:10,31; 3:15; Rev 6:12.\x* and¦34019 the moon¦34021 won't¦34022 shine at night.\wj*\x + \xo 13:24: \xt Isa 13:10; Eze 32:7.\x*
\v 25 \wj The¦34028 stars¦34029 will fall¦34036 down out¦34032 of the sky¦34034\x + \xo 13:25: \xt Isa 34:4; Rev 6:13.\x* and¦34039 the powers¦34041 in¦34043 the heavens¦34047 will be¦34050 shaken¦34050 up.\wj*\x + \xo 13:25: \xt Yoel 2:10.\x*
\v 26 \wj Then¦34051 the people will¦34053 see¦34053 the son¦34055 of¦34057 humanity in¦34060 the clouds¦34062 coming¦34058 with¦34065 incredible power¦34066 and¦34068 brightness.\wj*\x + \xo 13:26: \xt Dan 7:13; Rev 1:7.\x*
\v 27 \wj He'll send¦34073 the messengers¦34076 out¦34073 to collect all the chosen¦34082 people from the four¦34086 corners of¦34083 the world, from everywhere between the earth¦34092 and¦34078 the sky.\wj*
\s1 Watch out for the change in season
