\r (Mat. 24:32-35; Luke 21:29-33)
\p
\v 28 “\wj So¦34099 learn¦34102 a lesson from fig¦34101 trees—whenever¦34105 the branches¦34109 green up and start sprouting¦34114 leaves¦34116 and then¦34099 everyone knows¦34119 that¦34121 summer¦34125 is¦34126 close.\wj*
\v 29 \wj So too whenever¦34130 you see¦34132 all these¦34134 things happening, you know¦34139 that¦34141 the end \+add of this current world\+add* is¦34143 close.\wj*
\v 30 \wj I can assure you¦34149 that¦34156 the¦34154 generation¦34155 of people who see these things won't¦34152 die off before these latter things happen.\wj*
\v 31 \wj The sky and¦34167 the planet might collapse, but¦34173 my¦34175 teachings will never become irrelevant.\wj*
\s1 Stay alert for the coming of the master
\rem /s1 The Day and Hour Unknown; The Necessity for Watchfulness; No One Knows the Day or Hour
\r (Mat. 24:36-44)
\p
\v 32 “\wj But as for the date or¦34185 time when all this will happen, only the father¦34205 knows that—even the son¦34201 and messengers¦34193 don't¦34191 know.\wj*\x + \xo 13:32: \xt Mat 24:36.\x*
\v 33 \wj So watch out¦34206, observe current events, and¦34210 be praying¦34211, because¦34214 you¦34213 won't¦34212 know¦34213 exactly when all this will happen.\wj*
\v 34 \wj It¦34230 can all be compared to a man¦34229 who was about to leave his house¦34234 and go on a trip. Before he leaves, he gives certain jobs and responsibilities to his various slaves¦34240, and instructs his security guard to stay alert.\wj*\x + \xo 13:34: \xt Luk 12:36-38.\x*
\v 35 \wj So¦34257 you¦34259 all¦34259 watch¦34256 and stay alert, because¦34260 you don't¦34258 know¦34259 when¦34261 the master¦34263 of¦34264 the house¦34265 might return—perhaps one evening¦34268 or at midnight¦34271, or at dawn or maybe mid-morning.\wj*
\v 36 \wj You¦34281 certainly don't want to be caught napping when he¦34280 comes¦34278.\wj*
\v 37 \wj And what¦34284 I'm telling you¦34287 now, I tell¦34288 everyone: stay alert and¦34286 watch¦34292.\wj*”
\c 14
