\p
\v 1 Now it was¦34293 two¦34301 days¦34302 before the Passover¦34296 Feast¦34296 and the \it Flat Bread¦34299 Celebration\it*, and the chief¦34306 priests¦34306 and the religious¦34310 teachers¦34310 were¦34304 trying to figure out how¦34311 they could have Yeshua set up so they could arrest him and have him executed,\x + \xo 14:1: \xt Exo 12:1-27.\x*
\v 2 but they¦34319 knew that the Feast¦34326 wouldn't be¦34329 a good time because¦34320 the people¦34332 would protest \add in Yeshua's favour\add*.
\s1 The woman anoints Yeshua for his burial
\rem /s1 Jesus Is Anointed at Bethany; The Anointing at Bethany
\r (Yhn 12:1-8; Mat. 26:6-13)
\p
\v 3 Meanwhile, Yeshua was in Beyt-Ania¦34339 \add !(Bethany¦34339)\add* at the home of Simon¦34343 who had previously had leprosy¦34345. Yeshua was sitting¦34346 there when a woman¦34349 came¦34348 in with a hand-crafted container of very expensive¦34357 fragrant oil. Breaking open the sealed flask¦34364, she¦34367 poured¦34367 the fragrant oil over Yeshua's head¦34372.\x + \xo 14:3: \xt Luk 7:37-38.\x*
\v 4 Immediately some¦34377 started quietly grumbling about the extravagant waste,
\v 5 then¦34414 they¦34415 scolded the woman because¦34399 a flask of genuine lotion like this could easily fetch almost a year's wages if it was¦34398 sold¦34405.
\p
\v 6 But \nd Yeshua\nd* spoke up, “\wj What do you think you're doing abusing her—leave her alone! She's¦34433 done something very good¦34430 for me.\wj*
\v 7 \wj You'll always¦34438 have poor¦34441 people around, and¦34446 you can help them whenever¦34447 you want¦34448 to, but¦34446 I won't¦34458 be around forever.\wj*\x + \xo 14:7: \xt Deu 15:11.\x*
\v 8 \wj She has¦34462 performed the¦34470 traditional anointing¦34468 of my body¦34471 in advance of my burial¦34475.\wj*
\v 9 \wj And I can assure you¦34479 that¦34495 wherever¦34481 the good¦34486 news is proclaimed¦34484 around the world¦34491, what she has done¦34494 today will be part of the story and¦34477 she'll be remembered for it.\wj*”
