\r (Yhn 13:21-30; Mat. 26:17-25; Luke 22:7-14, 21-23)
\p
\v 12 On¦34541 the first¦34542 day¦34543 of¦34545 the \it Flat Bread¦34545 Celebration\it* when¦34546 the lambs would be slaughtered ready for the special Passover meal, Yeshua's apprentices¦34553 asked him, “Where¦34555 do you want¦34556 us to get everything ready for our Passover meal?”
\p
\v 13 So¦34564 Yeshua sent¦34565 off two¦34567 of them¦34577 with these instructions, “\wj Go into town¦34582 and¦34564 a man¦34588 carrying a pitcher¦34589 of water¦34590 will meet¦34586 you¦34587 there. Just follow¦34592 him\wj*
\v 14 \wj until he goes into a house. Then¦34594 find the owner¦34601 of the house and tell¦34605 him that¦34602 the teacher¦34604 wants to know the location of the guestroom¦34609 where¦34595 he and his apprentices¦34616 can celebrate the Passover¦34613 meal.\wj*
\v 15 \wj He'll show¦34625 you a large¦34628, furnished¦34629 room¦34626 upstairs¦34626—that's where you can get everything ready¦34631.\wj*”
\p
\v 16 So¦34637 the two of them went¦34638 off into¦34650 the town¦34652, and everything happened there exactly as¦34656 Yeshua had told them, and so they¦34660 prepared¦34660 the special meal there.
\s1 Yeshua shocks his apprentices at the Passover meal
\r (Yhn 13:21-30; Mat. 26:20-30; Luke 22:14-23; 1 Cor. 11:23-25)
\p
\v 17 As the evening¦34664 approached, Yeshua went in for dinner with his twelve¦34671 apprentices.
\v 18 As they were sitting¦34673 around eating, he told them, “\wj I'll tell¦34683 you frankly that¦34685 one¦34686 of¦34687 you eating with me here will hand me over \+add to be arrested\+add*.\wj*”\x + \xo 14:18: \xt Psa 41:9.\x*
\v 19 That upset them, and¦34703 several of them individually asked, “Surely¦34710 it couldn't be me?”
\p
\v 20 Then¦34719 he¦34718 continued¦34721, “\wj It's one of¦34726 you twelve¦34727—the one who dips his bread in the sauce at the same time as me.\wj*
\v 21 \wj Indeed it's written¦34749 \+add in the scriptures\+add* that the son¦34742 of humanity will be arrested, but on the other¦34754 hand¦34754, what a tragedy it'll be for the one who hands him over—in fact it would be better¦34765 for that man¦34773 if he was¦34771 never born.\wj*”
\rem /s1 The Lord's Supper; The Institution of the Lord's Supper; Communion
\rem /r (Matthew 26.26-30; Luke 22.14-20; 1 Corinthians 11.23-25)
\p
\v 22 As they carried on eating¦34776, he took¦34778 some bread, blessed¦34782 \add God\add*, broke¦34785 it apart and¦34775 gave¦34788 a piece to¦34790 them¦34790, saying¦34792, “\wj Take this¦34796 bread—it's¦34785 my¦34800 body¦34799.\wj*”
\p
\v 23 Then¦34801 he¦34806 picked up a cup¦34804, gave¦34806 thanks¦34805 \add to God\add*, and¦34801 passed it around so they could each drink from it,
\v 24 saying¦34816, “\wj This is¦34819 the blood¦34821 of my¦34822 contract\x + \xo 14:24: \xt Exo 24:8.\x* that¦34827 will be poured¦34831 out¦34831 for¦34832 many¦34833 \+add people\+add*.\wj*\x + \xo 14:24: \xt Jer 31:31-34.\x*
\v 25 \wj I can assure you¦34839 that¦34840 I won't¦34843 drink anything made from grapes until¦34852 I drink new¦34859 juice in¦34860 God's kingdom¦34862.\wj*”
\rem /s1 Peter's Denial Foretold
\p
\v 26 And after they'd sung¦34866 some songs, they left¦34867 the town and¦34865 went¦34867 across to¦34868 the Mount¦34870 of¦34872 Olives¦34872.
\s1 Yeshua predicts Peters denials
\rem /s1 Jesus Predicts Peter's Denial
\r (Yhn 13:36-38; Mat. 26:31-35; Luke 22:31-34)
\p
\v 27 Then¦34874 \nd Yeshua\nd* continued his teaching, “\wj All¦34882 of you¦34882 will stumble¦34882 because¦34891 it's¦34892 written¦34892 in the scriptures: ‘I'll¦34893 strike¦34893 down the shepherd¦34895 and¦34896 the sheep¦34900 will be¦34902 scattered¦34902.’\wj*\x + \xo 14:27: \xt Zech 13:7.\x*
\v 28 \wj But after¦34905 I come back to life, I'll¦34911 go¦34911 on ahead of you¦34912 back to Galilee¦34915.\wj*”\x + \xo 14:28: \xt Mat 28:16.\x*
\p
\v 29 But¦34917 Peter¦34918 contradicted him¦34922, “Even¦34926 if¦34924 everyone else stumbles¦34928, I won't¦34931!”
\p
\v 30 “\wj I can assure you,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* responded, “\wj that¦34947 you'll renounce¦34961 me three¦34957 times this¦34947 very night¦34949, before¦34951 the rooster¦34954 crows early tomorrow morning.\wj*”
\p
\v 31 But¦34989 Peter argued forcibly, “Even if I had to¦34980 die¦34980 with¦34981 you, I would never disown you!”
\p And all¦34991 the others said¦34970 similar things.
\s1 Yeshua, in distress, prays at Gethsemane
\rem /s1 Jesus Prays in Gethsemane
\r (Mat. 26:36-46; Luke 22:39-46)
\p
\v 32 They¦34995 walked along until¦35011 they¦34995 came¦34995 to a piece of¦34998 land called Gethsemane¦35002 where Yeshua told his¦35008 apprentices¦35007 to sit down¦35009 while he prayed.
\v 33 He¦35015 took¦35015 Peter¦35017 and Yacob¦35020 and Yohan¦35023 further in with¦35024 him¦35025 where he stared off in a daze but¦35014 was obviously very distressed¦35031.
\v 34 He¦35034 told the three of them, “\wj My¦35040 soul¦35039 is¦35037 deathly¦35042 sad! You guys just stay here¦35044 and¦35045 keep alert.\wj*”
\p
\v 35 He went ahead a little¦35050 way, where he¦35052 knelt on¦35055 the¦35056 ground¦35058 with his head down and¦35047 prayed¦35061—asking if it¦35065 was possible¦35064 to avoid what was ahead of him¦35070.
\v 36 But¦35074 he¦35075 said¦35075, “\wj Father, I know that¦35091 you can do anything. Let me avoid this suffering, but yes I do know, it doesn't matter what I want¦35105 but rather what you've \+add planned\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 37 Then¦35107 he went back and¦35107 found¦35110 the¦35115 others sleeping¦35112. “\wj Simon¦35117, are you asleep?\wj*” he asked Peter¦35116. “\wj Couldn't you stay awake even for a single hour¦35123?\wj*
\v 38 \wj You¦35130 all¦35130 need to stay alert and¦35126 be¦35127 careful not¦35129 to give into¦35132 temptation¦35133. I know your spirits¦35136 are enthusiastic on one hand, but¦35126 it's still easy to give in to the moment.\wj*”
\p
\v 39 Then¦35142 he¦35145 went further in again and¦35142 prayed¦35145 as before,
\v 40 but when he returned again¦35151, he found¦35154 them all asleep because¦35159 they were tired, but they couldn't really find any excuse to¦35174 give.
\p
\v 41 The¦35177 third¦35178 time that Yeshua returned, he¦35176 said¦35180 to them¦35181, “\wj Ah, you're all¦35182 sleeping¦35182 again and¦35175 having a good rest¦35184. It's well earned but¦35175 the time has come for¦35183 the son¦35199 of¦35201 humanity to be handed over¦35197 to evil men.\wj*
\v 42 \wj Come on—get up—we¦35208 need to go¦35208! Look¦35209, the¦35211 one who'll hand me¦35214 over¦35212 is on his way.\wj*”
\s1 Yeshua is arrested in the night
\rem /s1 Jesus Arrested; Jesus Is Betrayed and Arrested; The Arrest of Jesus; The Betrayal and Arrest of Jesus
\r (Yhn 18:3-12; Mat. 26:47-56; Luke 22:47-53)
\p
\v 43 Even while Yeshua was still¦35219 speaking¦35221, Yudas¦35224 reached him, followed by a crowd¦35234 from the chief¦35243 priests¦35243, the religious¦35247 teachers¦35247, and the elders¦35250—many armed with swords¦35237 and clubs¦35239.
\v 44 Yudas had¦35251 prearranged a signal¦35258 with them¦35259 that anyone who he¦35265 greeted with a kiss¦35264, they should grab that person and¦35253 lead¦35271 him¦35268 away¦35271 under guard.
\p
\v 45 So¦35275 he walked right up to Yeshua and said¦35281, “My honoured teacher,” and greeted him¦35288 with a kiss.
\v 46 Then¦35290 the¦35294 others with him grabbed Yeshua and¦35290 secured him.
\v 47 But¦35321 one¦35305 of the ones with Yeshua that was beside him¦35323, drew¦35310 his¦35323 sword¦35312 and¦35321 struck¦35315 a slave¦35318 of the chief¦35320 priest¦35320, cutting¦35322 off¦35322 the man's ear¦35325.
\v 48 \nd Yeshua\nd* spoke to the¦35328 crowd, “\wj Did you¦35336 all¦35336 bring swords¦35338 and¦35339 clubs¦35340 to try to capture¦35341 me¦35342 like you'd chase down a thief?\wj*
\v 49 \wj I was¦35345 standing there teaching¦35351 in the¦35349 temple¦35350 every¦35343 day¦35344 and¦35352 you¦35354 could¦35359 have arrested me¦35356, but¦35352 it's¦35357 happened this way to ensure that what's written in scriptures¦35361 will be¦35359 fulfilled¦35359.\wj*”\x + \xo 14:49: \xt Luk 19:47; 21:37.\x*
\p
\v 50 Meanwhile, the others who'd been with Yeshua had¦35369 taken off.
\v 51 One young¦35377 fellow was¦35380 wearing a single linen¦35386 robe, and¦35374 when the crowd tried to grab him,
\v 52 it came off \add in the struggle\add* and¦35399 he ran away stark naked¦35404.
\s1 The mock trial where Yeshua is sentenced to death
\rem /s1 Jesus before the Council; Before the Sanhedrin
\r (Yhn 18:13-14,19-24; Mat. 26:57-68; Luke 22:54-55,63-71)
\p
\v 53 The guards led¦35409 \nd Yeshua\nd* away¦35409 to¦35412 the chief priest's¦35414 residence, and all¦35422 the chief priests¦35424 and the elders¦35429 and the religious¦35433 teachers¦35433 gathered there also.
\v 54 Peter¦35436 followed¦35439 along from¦35437 a distance and¦35434 went in as far¦35442 as the courtyard¦35446 of¦35447 the residence where he¦35450 joined the servants who were sitting¦35452 around the fire¦35461 keeping warm.
\v 55 Inside, the chief¦35464 priests¦35464 and¦35463 all¦35466 the council¦35468 were trying to establish a case against¦35470 \nd Yeshua\nd* so he could be sentenced to death¦35478, but¦35463 they¦35483 weren't coming up with anything.
\v 56 Several people were¦35486 making up charges against¦35488 him¦35489, but¦35490 none of the¦35492 accusers' stories agreed with each other.
\p
\v 57 Eventually some¦35498 of them stood¦35499 up¦35499 and¦35496 offered this false¦35500 charge:
\v 58 “We heard¦35508 him¦35509 say¦35510 that¦35518 he would demolish this¦35518 temple¦35517 made¦35527 by many labourers, and within three¦35523 days¦35524 he'd build¦35528 another¦35525 one without any helpers.”\x + \xo 14:58: \xt Yhn 2:19.\x*
\v 59 But¦35529 even then¦35529, they couldn't get their¦35537 accusations to align with each other.
\p
\v 60 Nevertheless the chief¦35541 priest¦35541 in¦35542 the middle of the council stood¦35539 up and¦35538 asked¦35545 \nd Yeshua\nd*, “Aren't you going to defend yourself? These¦35554 men¦35554 are¦35556 accusing you of these¦35554 things.”
\p
\v 61 But¦35564 Yeshua didn't¦35565 say¦35580 anything. So the chief¦35573 priest¦35573 asked¦35574 again, “Is¦35580 it true that you're the \nd chosen¦35587\nd* one that God promised to send—the son¦35589 of the blessed¦35593 \add God\add*?”
\p
\v 62 “\wj I am.\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* replied, “\wj and you'll¦35605 all¦35605 see¦35605 the son¦35607 of¦35609 humanity sitting¦35613 in the honoured position by the powerful¦35615 God and¦35616 coming¦35617 through the clouds¦35621 in the sky¦35624.\wj*”\x + \xo 14:62: \xt Dan 7:13.\x*
\p
\v 63 Then¦35626 the chief¦35627 priest¦35627 tore¦35629 his own robe \add to show his disgust\add* and¦35626 shouted, “We¦35638 certainly don't need¦35637 any more witnesses¦35639 now!
\v 64 You¦35652 yourselves all¦35652 heard¦35642 him¦35662 insult God. What sentence does that deserve?”\x + \xo 14:64: \xt Lev 24:16.\x*
\p So¦35658 the¦35656 leaders there agreed that Yeshua needed to be¦35666 sentenced to death¦35667.
\p
\v 65 Then¦35668 various people started¦35669 spitting¦35671 on¦35672 him, and blindfolding¦35674 him and beating¦35682 him saying¦35686, “Ha, tell¦35686 us who that was!” Even the servants joined in to slap him.
\s1 Peter disowns Yeshua
\rem /s1 Peter Denies Jesus
\r (Yhn 18:15-18,25-27; Mat. 26:69-75; Luke 22:56-62)
\p
\v 66 Meanwhile, Peter¦35709 was down in¦35711 the courtyard¦35713 when one¦35718 of the chief¦35723 priest's¦35723 servant¦35720 girls¦35720 came¦35715 out,
\v 67 and seeing¦35725 Peter¦35727 warming¦35728 himself¦35728, she¦35732 looked more closely and said¦35732, “Hey, you were¦35742 with¦35735 that \nd Yeshua\nd* from \nd Nazareth¦35740\nd*!”
\p
\v 68 But¦35760 he denied it¦35748, “I don't know him and¦35760 I don't know why you¦35756 think I would!” And he moved away from the¦35764 fire.
\p
\v 69 But¦35775 the girl¦35777 that had seen¦35778 him¦35779 said¦35789 to some of the others standing¦35792 around, “That¦35793 guy's one of them¦35798.”
\p
\v 70 But¦35805 again Peter¦35814 denied it.
\p A little¦35807 while later, some of those standing¦35810 there said¦35812, “You¦35818 must be one of them because¦35820 you're¦35818 from Galilee¦35821.”
\p
\v 71 Now Peter started¦35830 swearing¦35834 and cursing¦35831 and said, “I've¦35837 never even met that fellow that you're all¦35842 talking¦35842 about!”
\p
\v 72 Right then¦35843 the rooster crowed for the second¦35846 time¦35846 and Peter¦35853 remembered¦35850 now what Yeshua had¦35879 told him¦35862—how he would renounce¦35876 Yeshua three¦35874 times before the rooster crowed—and he broke¦35879 down and cried.
\c 15
\s1 Pilate tries to interrogate Yeshua
\rem /s1 Jesus Before Pilate; Jesus' Trial before Pilate
\r (Yhn 18:28-38; Mat. 27:1-2,11-14; Luke 23:1-5)
\p
\v 1 First thing in¦35887 the morning¦35887, the chief¦35893 priests¦35893 called a meeting with¦35894 the elders¦35896 and the religious¦35900 teachers¦35900 and all¦35903 the council¦35905, and they ordered that \nd Yeshua\nd* be tied¦35907 up and taken over¦35916 to¦35919 Governor Pilate¦35919.
\v 2 There Pilate¦35924 asked¦35921 him¦35922, “Are you¦35926 the king¦35929 of¦35930 the Jews?”
\p “\wj You said¦35938 it¦35940,\wj*” replied Yeshua.
\p
\v 3 Then¦35941 the¦35945 chief¦35946 priests¦35946 started hurling accusations¦35942 against¦35944 Yeshua,
\v 4 so Pilate¦35954 asked¦35956 him¦35958 again¦35955, “Don't¦35961 you have anything to say¦35960? Listen¦35964 to all these accusations¦35968 they're making against¦35966 you.”
\p
\v 5 But Pilate¦35979 was astounded that \nd Yeshua\nd* didn't answer¦35975 any further.
\s1 Pilate agrees to execute an innocent man
\rem /s1 Jesus Is Sentenced to Death; Pilate Hands Jesus over to Be Crucified
\r (Yhn 18:39–19:16; Mat. 27:15-26; Luke 23:13-25)
\p
\v 6 Now at time of the¦35983 Jewish Passover, Pilate would normally pardon one prisoner¦35991 for them and¦35981 release him.
\v 7 There was another prisoner at the time named Barabbas¦36003 who¦36009 was an activist accused of murder¦36013.
\v 8 By now, the¦36021 crowd¦36022 had¦36019 arrived and¦36017 asked Pilate to¦36024 release a prisoner as¦36026 usual at Passover,
\v 9 so he asked them¦36036, “Do you want¦36038 me to release the King¦36043 of¦36044 the Jews for you?”
\v 10 (This was because Pilate was well aware that¦36051 the¦36057 chief¦36058 priests¦36058 had¦36054 brought Yeshua because they were jealous of¦36052 his \add popularity\add*.)
\v 11 But the chief¦36061 priests¦36061 stirred¦36063 up¦36063 the crowd¦36066 to start saying that it was Barabbas¦36072 that they wanted released,
\v 12 so Pilate¦36077 asked again¦36078, “Then¦36076 what¦36084 should I do¦36087 with this man that¦36088 you¦36089 call¦36089 the King¦36091 of¦36093 the Jews?”
\p
\v 13 The crowd yelled¦36098 back, “Execute¦36101 him¦36102 on¦36101 a pole.”
\p
\v 14 “What¦36108 has he¦36111 even done¦36111 wrong?” Pilate¦36105 demanded.
\p But¦36104 they¦36113 just yelled¦36117 louder, “Execute¦36120 him¦36121 on¦36120 a pole!”
\p
\v 15 Now Pilate¦36124 wanted to placate the crowd¦36127, so he had Barabbas¦36138 released while he had \nd Yeshua\nd* flogged¦36145 and¦36123 then¦36123 handed over to the execution¦36148 squad.
\s1 The battalion plays with their mock ‘king’
\rem /s1 The Soldiers Make Fun of Jesus; The Soldiers Mock Jesus
\r (Yhn 19:2-3; Mat. 27:27-31)
\p
\v 16 So¦36150 the soldiers¦36151 led¦36152 Yeshua inside the palace¦36158 that¦36160 was the governor's¦36162 residence¦36162, and¦36163 called¦36165 in the rest of¦36162 the battalion.
\v 17 They¦36170 \add mocked Yeshua\add* by dressing¦36170 him¦36172 in¦36170 a kingly robe, and¦36169 after someone twisted¦36178 some thorns¦36179 together¦36178 into a mock crown¦36180, they¦36176 pressed it onto his head,
\v 18 and¦36181 began¦36182 saluting him¦36184, “Greetings¦36187, king¦36190 of¦36191 the¦36191 Jews.”
\v 19 They¦36194 took turns whacking his¦36195 head¦36200 with¦36202 a stick and spitting¦36204 on¦36206 him, while others knelt¦36208 down in front of him and pretended to be bowing to him.
\v 20 After they'd finished having fun mocking¦36215 him, they took the purple¦36220 robe off¦36217 him, and¦36213 put his¦36227 own¦36225 robe back on him. Then¦36213 they led¦36232 him outside towards the execution¦36235 spot.
\s1 Yeshua is publicly executed along with thieves
\rem /s1 The Crucifixion of Jesus; Jesus Is Crucified
\r (Yhn 19:17-27; Mat. 27:32-44; Luke 23:26-43)
\p
\v 21 As they walked out of the city, they came¦36247 across a man¦36241 coming¦36247 in from the country¦36250. He was Simon¦36243 from Cyrene¦36246, the father¦36252 of Alexander¦36253 and Rufus¦36255, and the soldiers forced him¦36260 to carry¦36257 the execution¦36259 pole,\x + \xo 15:21: \xt Rom 16:13.\x*
\v 22 and¦36261 so they¦36263 all arrived at Golgotha¦36268 (which¦36270 means ‘Place¦36275 of the skull¦36275’).
\v 23 There the soldiers went to give¦36278 some spiced wine¦36282 to Yeshua, but¦36286 he¦36288 declined it.
\v 24 So¦36289 they¦36294 carried out the¦36296 execution¦36290, taking¦36306 Yeshua's clothes¦36297 and¦36304 drawing straws to see who¦36304 would get what.\x + \xo 15:24: \xt Psa 22:18.\x*
\v 25 By now it¦36307 was¦36307 around 9am, and¦36312 they¦36314 affixed Yeshua to the¦36309 pole.
\v 26 The charge¦36322 had¦36324 been written out and¦36316 attached \add at the top\add*: “The king¦36328 of the Jews.”
\v 27 That morning, two¦36337 thieves were also executed¦36334 there—one on each side of¦36348 Yeshua.
\p
\v 28 ◘
\v 29 As people passed¦36362 by on the path, they insulted Yeshua, shaking¦36365 their¦36368 heads¦36367\x + \xo 15:29: \xt Psa 22:7; 109:25.\x* and shouting, “Hoy there! You¦36373 who reckoned you¦36373 could demolish the temple¦36376 and rebuild it¦36378 in¦36379 three¦36380 days¦36381,\x + \xo 15:29: \xt Yhn 2:19; Mrk 14:58.\x*
\v 30 come¦36387 down¦36387 from¦36388 that pole and save¦36383 yourself¦36384.”
\p
\v 31 Similarly¦36391 the chief¦36395 priests¦36395 and the religious¦36402 teachers¦36402 laughed together and mocked¦36396, “He did miracles for others¦36404, but he can't¦36407 even save¦36409 himself¦36406.
\v 32 Now¦36417 if that¦36421 so-called ‘\nd chosen¦36411\nd* one’ or ‘king¦36413 of¦36415 Yisrael¦36415’ would just come¦36416 down¦36416 from¦36418 there, \em then¦36427\em* we'd be able to believe¦36425 him¦36431.”
\p Even the¦36428 other two being executed¦36429 with him were¦36432 deriding¦36432 him.
\s1 Yeshua breathes his last
\rem /s1 The Death of Jesus
\r (Yhn 19:28-30; Mat. 27:45-56; Luke 23:44-49)
\p
\v 33 At noon, it got dark everywhere, until¦36448 around 3pm,
\v 34 when \nd Yeshua\nd* shouted¦36458 loudly¦36462, “\wj My¦36475 god, my¦36475 god, why¦36480 have you¦36482 abandoned¦36482 me?\wj*”\x + \xo 15:34: \xt Psa 22:1.\x*
\p
\v 35 Some¦36486 of¦36487 the people standing¦36490 nearby thought he¦36497 was calling¦36497 the prophet Eliyah¦36496 \add !(Elijah¦36496)\add*.
\v 36 One of them ran¦36500, and soaked a sponge¦36507 in some sour wine¦36508, then¦36501 put¦36510 it on a stick and held it up for Yeshua to drink¦36513, saying¦36515, “Hang on. Let's see¦36519 if¦36520 Eliyah does come¦36521 to get him¦36524 down.”\x + \xo 15:36: \xt Psa 69:21.\x*
\p
\v 37 But¦36526 just then¦36526 \nd Yeshua¦36527\nd* uttered a loud¦36530 cry¦36529 and¦36526 exhaled his last breath.
\p
\v 38 (Back in the temple¦36536, the curtain¦36534 tore¦36537 down the middle from¦36542 the top¦36543 to¦36544 the bottom¦36545.)\x + \xo 15:38: \xt Exo 26:31-33.\x*
\v 39 When¦36547 Yeshua died, the¦36548 Roman centurion¦36549 who had been standing¦36551 back watching everything said¦36564, “This¦36566 man¦36568 was¦36573 definitely God's son¦36571.”
\p
\v 40 Further back, there was also¦36578 a group of women¦36579 observing¦36582 everything. These included Maria from Magdala¦36589, Maria the mother¦36600 of young Yacob and Yoses, and Salome¦36602,\x + \xo 15:40-41: \xt Luk 8:2-3.\x*
\v 41 and others who had followed¦36610 Yeshua around Galilee¦36609 and helped look after¦36612 him, along with many¦36620 others who had come¦36622 down to Yerushalem¦36625 with him.
\s1 Yosef boldly lays the body in a burial chamber
\rem /s1 The Burial of Jesus
\r (Yhn 19:38-42; Mat. 27:57-61; Luke 23:50-56)
\p
\v 42 As evening¦36628 came, it¦36632 was¦36632 now the Preparation¦36633 Day, i.e., the day before the Rest¦36636 Day.
\v 43 Yosef (who'd come¦36641 from¦36645 the city of Arimathea¦36646 and one who was¦36653 waiting¦36654 for¦36654 the coming of God's kingdom¦36656), a prominent¦36647 council¦36648 member¦36648, steeled himself¦36652 up and went¦36661 in¦36661 to see the governor to get permission to transfer \nd Yeshua's\nd* body¦36669.
\v 44 Governor Pilate¦36674 didn't think he'd be dead yet, so he called¦36683 an army commander to¦36683 find out if Yeshua had indeed died¦36691.
\v 45 As soon as he found out, he gave Yosef permission,
\v 46 so Yosef \add and his companions\add* went and bought¦36713 some linen¦36714 burial cloth and then¦36710, removing Yeshua's body from the pole, wrapped¦36721 it in the cloth and placed¦36729 it in a burial chamber that¦36737 had been¦36739 chiselled into a rockface. Then¦36710 they rolled¦36744 a rock¦36742 across the opening.
\v 47 Others were watching and noted where¦36772 the body had¦36773 been laid¦36773, including¦36760 Maria from Magdala¦36759 and Maria who was Yoses' mother¦36762.
\c 16
\s1 The massive shock at the burial chamber
\rem /s1 The Resurrection of Jesus
\r (Yhn 20:1-10; Mat. 28:1-8; Luke 24:1-12)
\p
\v 1 After the Rest Day was over, Maria from¦36783 Magdala¦36783 and Maria the mother¦36786 of¦36788 Yacob and Salome¦36790, went and bought¦36792 some traditional burial spices¦36793 that evening to take to the burial chamber and place with the body.
\v 2 Then¦36800 very early¦36803 on Sunday morning they¦36811 went to¦36812 the chamber, arriving just as the sun¦36820 was rising.
\v 3 But¦36821 they realised that they didn't have anyone with them to¦36823 roll the rock¦36835 away that was covering the entrance.
\v 4 However, when they looked¦36847 they saw that¦36852 the¦36857 very large¦36863 rock¦36860 had already been¦36854 rolled¦36854 away¦36854.
\v 5 So¦36866 they went on into the burial chamber and¦36866 were totally stunned to find a young¦36874 man¦36874 dressed in white¦36882, sitting¦36876 in there on the side.
\p
\v 6 He¦36886 assured them¦36890, “Don't¦36894 be surprised. I know you're looking¦36902 for¦36902 \nd Yeshua\nd* from \nd Nazareth¦36904\nd*, the one who was executed¦36907 on¦36907 a pole. But¦36888 see¦36912 there where¦36920 his body was—he's not¦36909 there because he came back to life.
\v 7 So you three should go and tell his¦36929 apprentices¦36928, and Peter¦36932 in particular, that he's going¦36924 to go up ahead of¦36929 them to Galilee¦36940 and you'll all see¦36944 him¦36943 up there¦36941, just as¦36945 he already told you.”\x + \xo 16:7: \xt Mat 26:32; Mrk 14:28.\x*
\p
\v 8 So¦36949 they¦36955 left the¦36957 chamber and took off running, still stunned and shaking and too scared to stop and to talk to anyone¦36969.
\rem It's not certain whether or not the following longer ending of this document was actually penned by the same author (Markos/Mark), or whether it was appended slightly later. Expert scholars are divided on this, and hence it's included here for your consideration:
\s1 \add The others don't believe that Maria saw Yeshua\add*
\rem /s1 AN OLD ENDING TO THE GOSPEL; THE LONGER ENDING OF MARK; Jesus Appears to Mary Magdalene
\r (Yhn 20:11-18; Mat. 28:9-10)
\rem /s2 [The most reliable early manuscripts and other ancient witnesses do not have Mark 16.9-20.]
\p
\v 9 \add After coming back to life early on Sunday morning, Yeshua appeared first to Maria from Magdala. (She was the one that he had once commanded seven demons to leave.)\add*
\v 10 \add After leaving him, she went and told his followers who were mourning and weeping at his loss.\add*
\v 11 \add But when she told them that he is alive again and that she'd seen him, they simply didn't believe her.\add*
\s1 \add Yeshua appears to two of his followers\add*
\rem /s1 Jesus Appears to Two Disciples; Jesus Appears to Two Followers
\r (Luke 24:13-35)
\p
\v 12 \add Later on, Yeshua appeared in a different form to two of his followers on the path as they left Yerushalem and headed out to the countryside,\add*
\v 13 \add but when they hurried back and told the others, no one believed them.\add*
\s1 \add Yeshua appears to his apprentices and instructs them\add*
\rem /s1 Jesus Appears to the Eleven; Jesus Commissions the Disciples
\r (Yhn 20:19-23; Mat. 28:16-20; Luke 24:36-49; Acts 1:6-8)
\p
\v 14 \add Later again when the eleven apprentices were sitting around eating, Yeshua appeared in the room and scolded them for not believing and for being so stubborn when they hadn't believed others who had told them that he'd come back from the dead.\add*
\v 15 \add Then he instructed them, “\+wj Travel around all the world\+wj*\add*\x + \xo 16:15: \xt Acts 1:8.\x* \add \+wj and tell everyone the good message.\+wj*\add*
\v 16 \add \+wj Anyone who believes and gets immersed in water will be saved, however, those who refuse to believe will be condemned to death.\+wj*\add*
\v 17 \add \+wj Those who believe will be able to do miracles: they'll be able to use my authority to command demons to leave and to speak new languages,\+wj*\add*
\v 18 \add \+wj and they'll be able to pick up snakes. If they drink anything poisonous, it won't hurt them, and they will place their hands on people and make them better.\+wj*”\add*
\s1 \add Yeshua is lifted up to heaven\add*
\rem /s1 The Ascension of Jesus; Jesus Is Taken Up to Heaven
\r (Luke 24:50-53; Acts 1:9-11)
\p
\v 19 \add When Yeshua had finished speaking, he was lifted up into heaven and seated in the honoured place\add*\x + \xo 16:19: \xt Acts 1:9-11.\x* \add next to God.\add*
\v 20 \add Then his followers went around preaching everywhere, and God worked through them and so they were able to confirm the truth of their preaching by doing miracles.\add*
